        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Saladin</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1137 CE – 1193 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1137 in Tikrit, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, to a family of Kurdish Rawadiya ancestry; son of Najm al-Din Ayyub, warden of the fortress of Tikrit</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">4 March 1193 (27 Safar 589 AH) at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, of a fever; buried in a mausoleum in the garden outside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-mosque">Umayyad Mosque</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">Vizier</a> of Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 26 March 1169; ruler of Egypt after the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> in 1171; declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Egypt and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> by the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> in 1175; founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid dynasty</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid dynasty</a>; abolishing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>; uniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> under one ruler; the victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Hattin</a> in 1187; the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>; the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>; a reputation for generosity in Muslim and Christian sources</span></div>
