    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Saladin rose in the service of the Zengid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a>, became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 1169 and two years later ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>.</li><li>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a>'s death in 1174 he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and then most of Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-mesopotamia">Upper Mesopotamia</a>, largely at the expense of his former master's family.</li><li>His victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Hattin</a> and capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1187 provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>, which ended in 1192 with Jerusalem still in his hands.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>At his death Saladin had in his possession one piece of gold and forty pieces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>; he had given away his wealth to his poor subjects and left nothing to pay for his funeral.</p></aside>
    </section>

